			<div class="content" id="post-content-1403701">
									

<p>I'm a little tardy to the party, but I have a fifth scenario.</p>
<p>-Everything is normal and unremarkable until key is inserted. When key is inserted, lights dim but everything else is observable and normal. Once the unlocked door clears the frame, the room is suddenly, and without transistion, a crime scene. In the recordings, there is simply a jump, like bad editing, but of course no evidence of editing or tampering with the footage can be found.</p>
<p>My thinking is that the effect only occurs at that particular instant, so there is nothing untoward to observe externaly until that instant. Either the effect just transmutes the interior into evidence that seems several hours old, or the effect is retro-active in time but constrained to the unlocked area.</p>

